Z||000000||GTFiero1||10-14-2001||08:25 PM||||anyone here like American Motots cars? i always liked them. the AMX is sweet and i really like the "Rebel Machine" . <A HREF="http://www.arcticboy.com" TARGET=_blank>www.arcticboy.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000001||loafer87gt||10-14-2001||08:33 PM||||I really liked the AMX as well. One of the guys I used to work with had an AMC Spirit. It had a 4.2 litre straight six but the engine was an absolute dog. To put things in perspective, my brothers 1.6 Honda engine made more HP and almost as much torque as the beast. The courier who delivered stuff at our office used to have a Spirit as well but his was an AMX. It had an AMC made 302 in it that supposedly went like stink.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||10-14-2001||09:33 PM||||I have a jeep that was made by AMC. It's such a conglomeration of different company's parts, you never know what to buy. Still haven't figured out who built the eng. Ford ign components, gm suspension/steering, a mixture of drive train parts. Interior is junk, all pooly matched plastic. The 4wd is tuff, tho awkward. A vac motor shifts a yoke/sliding colar to couple the right wheel to the rest of the drive axle.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||10-15-2001||01:38 AM||||I love the AMX as well.  I think this is basically their only car that really was a hit with more than a handful of people.  I may be wrong, but I think it was their only "real" vehicle.  It's a lot like international harvester; they made a lot of stuff, but the scout (early ones) was a very cool and durable rig...and I don't have much use for tractors and 3 tons <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I stumbled across something the other day that Alabama state troopers had a 401 equipped AMX....lucky bastards!  How'd you like that to be your goverment supplied, fully paid for, insured, car? ha! hahahaha!  No way could that have been as cool as a caprice or crown vic, lol!  Oh, here's a link:<P> <A HREF="http://www.javelinamx.com/JavHome/copcar/copcar1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.javelinamx.com/JavHome/copcar/copcar1.htm</A> <P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||10-15-2001||01:43 AM||||I liked alot of AMC's cars just because they weren't your average Ford or Chevy.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Nashco||10-15-2001||01:48 AM||||Hmm..I just checked out the arctic boy link, and need to correct myself.  First of all, I always though a Javelin and an AMX were pretty much the same thing...I liked both of them.  I also didn't know that Nash was owned by AMC, and I do like the metropolitan convertibles.  I may be a little biased because my last name is Nash..hehe...but I do think the convertible were pretty cool.  Oh, and I see you already knew of the 'bama troopers, so no props to me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Anyway, I do like the AMX most of all, especially with the 401, very fun car!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||10-15-2001||08:33 AM||||i think at one time an amx was a javelin. i think amx is like a name that got applied to what ever they wanted to make sporty at a paticular time. like how "gto" got thrown on a couple of other pontiacs later on.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||10-15-2001||09:51 AM||||The first AMX was based on the Javelin, but had a shortened wheelbase, and no back seat. I had a friend who had one. 390, 4-speed. Pretty quick. <BR>The later AMX was only a performance package for the Javelin. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||10-15-2001||03:48 PM||||My alltime favorite AMC cars were the gremlin and pacer / aka the "goldfish bowl"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> 2 of the oddest eccono boxes ever built. <BR>A friend of mine had an embasador nicknamed "the bismark" due to its massive size and power. It was awesome blasting down the highway under full sail. You could hit a pothole and not feel it for 3 miles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
